[CENTER][SIZE=6][B]Expressive Launcher 5.1.9 QA (Build 82) — Don't Recycle What's Still on Screen[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][I]Official Release Announcement & Download Links[/I][/SIZE][/CENTER]

[HR][/HR]

5.1.9 fixes a Recents crash introduced in 5.1.8 (81) where Overview cards could throw [ICODE]Canvas: trying to use a recycled bitmap[/ICODE] after Android 17 delivered an updated task snapshot.

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]✨ What's New & Improved[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]1. 🛠️ Fix Recents recycled-bitmap crash (5.1.8 regression)[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Before[/B]: in 5.1.8 (81), [ICODE]RecentsModel.onTaskSnapshotChanged()[/ICODE] stopped unconditionally reporting snapshots as consumed, while [ICODE]TaskVisualsChangedDelegateImpl[/ICODE] (and [ICODE]RecentsView[/ICODE] on the legacy path) still returned [ICODE]null[/ICODE] after handing the incoming [ICODE]ThumbnailData[/ICODE] to [ICODE]TasksRepository[/ICODE]. Whenever Android 17 delivered an updated snapshot for a visible Recents card that was not currently in the 3-slot [ICODE]TaskThumbnailCache[/ICODE] (for example after LRU eviction, memory trim, or [ICODE]lastActiveTime[/ICODE] invalidation), [ICODE]TaskStackChangeListeners[/ICODE] immediately recycled the live [ICODE]Bitmap[/ICODE] right before [ICODE]TaskThumbnailView[/ICODE]'s [ICODE]FixedSizeImageView[/ICODE] drew it—crashing the launcher with [ICODE]Canvas: trying to use a recycled bitmap[/ICODE].
[*][B]Now[/B]: [ICODE]TaskVisualsChangeListener[/ICODE], [ICODE]TaskVisualsChangedDelegateImpl[/ICODE], [ICODE]TasksRepository[/ICODE], and [ICODE]RecentsView[/ICODE] accurately report [ICODE]true[/ICODE] whenever they retain a task snapshot, so live Recents card bitmaps are never prematurely recycled, while genuinely unused snapshots are still freed immediately.

[/LIST]
[SIZE=5][B]2. 🛡️ Defense-in-depth guards for Recents thumbnails[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Before[/B]: [ICODE]TaskUiStateMapper[/ICODE], [ICODE]TaskThumbnailView[/ICODE], [ICODE]TaskThumbnailCache[/ICODE], and [ICODE]TaskThumbnailViewDeprecated[/ICODE] only checked for [ICODE]null[/ICODE] bitmaps without checking [ICODE]isRecycled[/ICODE], and [ICODE]TaskThumbnailView.resetViews()[/ICODE] cleared its [ICODE]ImageView[/ICODE] with [ICODE]setImageBitmap(null)[/ICODE] (which still leaves an empty [ICODE]BitmapDrawable[/ICODE]).
[*][B]Now[/B]: all four layers guard against recycled bitmaps (falling back cleanly to the task's background color or a cache miss), and [ICODE]TaskThumbnailView.resetViews()[/ICODE] clears its drawable with [ICODE]setImageDrawable(null)[/ICODE].

[/LIST]
[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]😄 Launcher Humor[/B][/SIZE]

[QUOTE]♻️ [I]Being eco-friendly is great—just maybe wait until the Recents card is off screen before tossing its bitmap in the recycling bin.[/I][/QUOTE]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]💬 Community Notes[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Thanks[/B]: huge thanks to the Pixel 11 Pro XL tester on ExpressiveOS 1.3 who sent over the exact bug report and stack trace from [ICODE]5.1.8 (81)[/ICODE]—it pinpointed the 9-layer Recents view hierarchy and the regression immediately.
[*][B]Free Core & Developer Support[/B]: Expressive Core continues to ship all core daily-driver launcher functionality for free. Expressive Pro is available as a one-time $4.99 activation. Every dollar directly funds our ongoing tooling and infrastructure expenses—including automated CI/CD servers, dedicated Android 17 testing devices/emulators, signing pipelines, and active continuous development—keeping Expressive fast, independent, and completely ad-free.

[/LIST]
[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]🧩 Release Riddle[/B][/SIZE]

[QUOTE][I]I live in a tray of three, show you where you just were, and ruin the whole frame if someone recycles me too soon. What am I?[/I][/QUOTE]

[SPOILER="Tap to reveal answer"][B]A Recents task thumbnail![/B] 5.1.9 keeps active card bitmaps out of the recycling bin until nobody is drawing them. 🖼️[/SPOILER]

[HR][/HR]

